{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries"},"metadata":{"title":"Swift Package integration","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents-(lime)","category":"Orange Unified Design System"},"kind":"project","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries"]}],"sections":[{"backgroundImage":"ic_unified_ds.png","projectFiles":"OUDS-Lime-Tutorial.zip","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10,"kind":"hero","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several libraries for your needs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These libraries help to split products and make users able to select only what they need.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework for Apple platforms.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"title":"Swift Package integration","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","chapter":"Import of the Swift Package and choose its libraries","image":"ic_unified_ds.png"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Using Xcode, in your ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"project package dependencies"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", add a new ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Search with the GitHub repository URL (https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios), and select the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ouds-ios"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" dependency.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can then choose the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency rule"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" you want.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To know which version you need, you can have a look on the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/wiki\/01-%E2%80%90-Available-API"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and also the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/releases"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Let’s say you will use some release candidate version today, e.g. the version 3.0.0-rc.1","type":"text"}]}],"runtimePreview":null,"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-swift-package.png","code":null},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you downloaded the package, you will see several libraries are available."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They can be embedded inside your "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" libraries."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Things are separated to let users integrate only what they need and embed the bare minimum of content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesContract"}]},{"text":" library provides the main elements like the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSThemeableView"},{"type":"text","text":". The theme contract is defined inside it."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSThemesOrange","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesSosh"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" provides the theme implementation for the Sosh products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesWireframe"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" provides the theme implementation for the Wireframe theme, which is a theme dedicated to mockups and prototypes.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesOrangeCompact"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products but with constraints of sizes and spaces.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSComponents"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" contains the SwiftUI OUDS components defined with the Figma specifications, and also useful view modifers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSTokensRaw","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensSemantic"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensComponents"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" are libraries defining and providing the tokens for low level (raw),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"middle level (semantic) or component levels (high level).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSModules"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is for modules or rich components with extra logic.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSFoundations"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is dedicated to some utilities and shared logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-libraries.png","code":null,"type":"step","caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add for example only the umbrella product merging all products mentioned above: "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSSwiftUI"}],"type":"emphasis"}]}],"runtimePreview":null}],"contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS for iOS is an open source Swift Package available on GitHub under MIT license.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The package and the libraries must be added through Xcode.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"title":"Import the Swift Package and the libraries","anchor":"Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries"}]},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","assessments":[{"choices":[{"isCorrect":true,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"I can contribute to OUDS using pull request"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS is open source, under MIT license, and hosted on GitHub. Of course you can contribute!"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS supports officialy all Apple OS like visionOS, tvOS, watchOS, iPadOS, iOS and also CarPlay."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The main supported targets are iOS \/ iPadOS. However we do our best to support macOS, visionOS, tvOS and watchOS.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CarPlay specific cases are not scoped yet.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS provides UIKit components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS supports only SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which of these choices is correct?"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[]},{"choices":[{"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can import all products provided by the Swift Package, and tailor your choice to keep only the ones needed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Even if we recommend to choose only the atomic products you need, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSSwiftUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product wraps all of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":true,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some of the available products depending to my needs, or only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwiftUI"},{"text":" if I am very lazy and don’t care about my app size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You need to chose the products the Swift package provides.","type":"text"}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None, only the Swift package dependency matter.","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":false}],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which imports of the OUDS Swift Package products can I choose?"}]}],"content":[]}],"kind":"assessments"},{"action":{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Get started","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-2-intro","isActive":true},"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","kind":"callToAction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Welcome to the Lime theme tutorial! In this tutorial, you will learn how to create a custom OUDS theme by overriding tokens from the Orange theme."}],"title":"Introduction"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)\/$volume","doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-libraries"]],"modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-libraries","projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries","sections":[{"kind":"task","r